Three changes to ggml-opencl.cpp:

1. Lazy init in the buffer type. The OpenCL buffer type reads dev_ctx->backend_ctx in
get_alignment / get_max_size, which is only set once a backend (or alloc_buffer) has run
ggml_cl_init. mtmd now allocates the mmproj tensors from ggml_backend_dev_buffer_type()
before creating a backend (mtmd-model.cpp), which crashed on Adreno with a null backend_ctx.

2. Build the q3_k, q2_0, iq4_xs, iq1_s, iq1_m, iq3_s, iq3_xxs, iq2_s, iq2_xs and iq2_xxs
_q8_1_dp4a programs only when the device has cl_khr_integer_dot_product, like the other
dp4a programs in load_cl_kernels. On Adreno drivers without it (Adreno 630, Adreno 730 on
Snapdragon 8 Gen 1 / 8+ Gen 1) the build fails and build_program_from_source calls exit(1),
so the app dies on GPU init. Every dispatch site of these kernels already returns false
when has_integer_dot is unset, so the matmul falls back to the non-dp4a path.
scripts/__tests__/opencl-integer-dot-gate.test.ts fails when a sync adds an ungated one.

3. Decide GGML_OPENCL_ADRENO_USE_LARGE_BUFFER in ggml_cl_init, before kernel_compile_opts is
built: use it only when the device lists cl_qcom_large_buffer and a trivial kernel builds
with -qcom-enable-large-buffer. Upstream clears the flag later, in
ggml_opencl_print_backend_info, but kernel_compile_opts was already built with the option
and is never rebuilt. On a driver that rejects the option (Adreno 630: err -43,
"Unsupported OpenCL user option specified") every kernel build fails and the app exits.
